// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// Root-cause of the regression from 40.8% (attempt 1): the forbidden exact-equality
// delimiter check `next == "<<"` was replaced in attempt 71 with a forced-open span
// at budget end, which caused 29 malformed-content failures (repetition loops with
// large CloseSpanWithinBudget budgets) and 11 unclosed-span failures.
//
// Fix: restore attempt 1's proven structure but replace `next == "<<"` with
// `RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<")` after appending the token. This correctly
// handles space-prefixed tokens like `" <<"` and split delimiters.
//
// Strategy:
//   Phase 1 (all but last 4 steps): UnconstrainedStep; on RenderedEndsWith(generated,"<<")
//     call EnterObservedConstrainedSpan. Model naturally emits 4-5 spans per example.
//   Inside any span: AdaptiveConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken; close when
//     IsCompletePrefix; CloseSpanWithinBudget with ≤3 steps near budget end (no loop risk).
//   Budget pressure (maxSteps - steps ≤ 4 && steps > 0): force OpenConstrainedSpan
//     then CloseSpanWithinBudget(3) — tiny budget prevents repetition loops.
//   The evaluator extracts the LAST visible span, which is the final answer.
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// Invariant 1 — parser_validity:
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
//   Outside-span, UnconstrainedStep branch:
//     insideConstrainedOut starts false; we only flip it when RenderedEndsWith fires,
//     which calls EnterObservedConstrainedSpan setting currentConstrainedOut := [].
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by the method precondition. Otherwise
//     insideConstrainedOut stays false, making the implication vacuous.
//
//   Outside-span, force-open branch:
//     OpenConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := true, currentConstrainedOut := [].
//     parser.IsValidPrefix([]) holds by method precondition.
//
//   Inside-span, CloseConstrainedSpan branch:
//     Sets insideConstrainedOut := false, implication vacuously true.
//
//   Inside-span, CloseSpanWithinBudget branch:
//     Postcondition guarantees insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut) directly.
//
//   Inside-span, AdaptiveConstrainedStep branch:
//     Returns EOS or a parser-valid next token at currentConstrainedOut.
//     AppendConstrainedToken extends currentConstrainedOut by that token,
//     preserving IsValidPrefix by the token's parser validity.
//
// Invariant 2 — progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
//   Init: |generatedPrefix| + 0 = |generatedPrefix|. ✓
//
//   Outside-span, UnconstrainedStep (non-EOS): steps += 1, generated grows by 1.
//     |generated| + 1 <= |generatedPrefix| + steps + 1 = |generatedPrefix| + steps'. ✓
//   Outside-span, UnconstrainedStep (EOS): steps += 1, generated unchanged. ✓
//
//   Outside-span, OpenConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, generated grows by 1 ("<<").
//     |generated| + 1 <= |generatedPrefix| + steps + 1. ✓
//
//   Inside-span, CloseConstrainedSpan: steps += 1, generated grows by ≤1 (">>"). ✓
//
//   Inside-span, CloseSpanWithinBudget(closeBudget = maxSteps - steps):
//     Postcondition: |generatedOut| <= |generated| + closeBudget.
//     After steps := maxSteps: |generatedOut| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps = |generatedPrefix| + steps. ✓
//
//   Inside-span, AdaptiveConstrainedStep + AppendConstrainedToken:
//     steps += 1, generated grows by exactly 1. ✓
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

